# API Routes Skill

## Purpose
All backend API logic lives in `apps/api`. Routes follow REST conventions under `/api/v1/`. Every handler must be wrapped in `withApiHandler` — which composes CORS + DB connection + structured logging + Sentry error capture. This skill prevents bare handlers, unhandled errors, and inconsistent response shapes.

## Rules
1. **Every handler must be exported as `default withApiHandler(handler)`** — never export a bare handler.
2. **Always use the `sendAPIResponse` utility** for all responses — never call `res.json()` with a raw object.
3. **Use `apiStatusCodes` from `@/lib/constants`** — never hardcode HTTP status numbers.
4. **All handler logic lives inside a `switch(method)` block** — one function per HTTP verb, delegated to a named `handle*` function.
5. **Every error path must call `captureAPIError`** from `@/lib/utils/sentry` before responding.
6. **Input validation must happen before any DB call** — validate query params and body at the top of each handle function.
7. **DB calls must come from `@/lib/database` query functions** — never call Mongoose models directly inside route files.
8. **Admin routes must be wrapped with `withAdminHandler`** from `@/middleware/admin` — not `withApiHandler`.
9. **Use `firstQueryValue` from `@/lib/validation/queryParams`** to safely extract single query params.
10. **Never `throw` inside a handler** — catch errors, call `captureAPIError`, then respond with the appropriate status code.
11. **Rate limit sensitive endpoints** using `rateLimit` from `@/lib/utils/rateLimit`.

## Patterns

### Standard GET + POST handler
```ts
// apps/api/src/pages/api/v1/[resource]/index.ts
import type { NextApiRequest, NextApiResponse } from "next";
import { apiStatusCodes } from "@/lib/constants";
import { getResourceFromDB, createResourceInDB } from "@/lib/database";
import { sendAPIResponse } from "@/lib/utils";
import { captureAPIError } from "@/lib/utils/sentry";
import { firstQueryValue } from "@/lib/validation/queryParams";
import { withApiHandler } from "@/middleware/requestLogger";

const handler = async (req: NextApiRequest, res: NextApiResponse) => {
  const { method } = req;

  switch (method) {
    case "GET":
      return handleGetResource(req, res);
    case "POST":
      return handleCreateResource(req, res);
    default:
      return res.status(apiStatusCodes.METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED).json(
        sendAPIResponse({ status: false, message: "Method not allowed" }),
      );
  }
};

const handleGetResource = async (req: NextApiRequest, res: NextApiResponse) => {
  const id = firstQueryValue(req.query.id);

  if (!id) {
    return res.status(apiStatusCodes.BAD_REQUEST).json(
      sendAPIResponse({ status: false, message: "id is required" }),
    );
  }

  const { data, error } = await getResourceFromDB(id);

  if (error) {
    captureAPIError(error as Error, "/api/v1/resource", "GET", apiStatusCodes.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, { id });
    return res.status(apiStatusCodes.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR).json(
      sendAPIResponse({ status: false, error, message: "Error fetching resource" }),
    );
  }

  return res.status(apiStatusCodes.OKAY).json(sendAPIResponse({ status: true, data }));
};

const handleCreateResource = async (req: NextApiRequest, res: NextApiResponse) => {
  const { name, description } = req.body;

  if (!name) {
    return res.status(apiStatusCodes.BAD_REQUEST).json(
      sendAPIResponse({ status: false, message: "name is required" }),
    );
  }

  const { data, error } = await createResourceInDB({ name, description });

  if (error) {
    captureAPIError(error as Error, "/api/v1/resource", "POST", apiStatusCodes.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, { name });
    return res.status(apiStatusCodes.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR).json(
      sendAPIResponse({ status: false, error, message: "Error creating resource" }),
    );
  }

  return res.status(apiStatusCodes.CREATED).json(sendAPIResponse({ status: true, data }));
};

export default withApiHandler(handler);
```

### Admin-only route
```ts
// apps/api/src/pages/api/v1/admin/[resource].ts
import { withAdminHandler } from "@/middleware/admin";

const handler = async (req: NextApiRequest, res: NextApiResponse) => { /* ... */ };

export default withAdminHandler(handler);
```

### Route with DB disabled (health check, etc.)
```ts
export default withApiHandler(handler, { db: false });
```

## Anti-Patterns

### ❌ Bare handler export
```ts
// BAD
export default async function handler(req, res) {
  const data = await SomeModel.find();
  res.json({ data });
}
```
```ts
// GOOD
export default withApiHandler(async (req, res) => {
  const { data, error } = await getResourceFromDB();
  if (error) { captureAPIError(...); return res.status(500).json(...); }
  return res.status(200).json(sendAPIResponse({ status: true, data }));
});
```

### ❌ Direct Mongoose model import in route file
```ts
// BAD — models must not be used directly in route files
import UserModel from "@/lib/database/models/User";
const users = await UserModel.find();
```
```ts
// GOOD — use query functions
import { getUsersFromDB } from "@/lib/database";
const { data: users, error } = await getUsersFromDB();
```

### ❌ Hardcoded status codes
```ts
// BAD
res.status(200).json({ status: true });
res.status(500).json({ status: false });
```
```ts
// GOOD
import { apiStatusCodes } from "@/lib/constants";
res.status(apiStatusCodes.OKAY).json(sendAPIResponse({ status: true, data }));
res.status(apiStatusCodes.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR).json(sendAPIResponse({ status: false, error }));
```
